}

^["interaction_depth"]{
 subjects: [#preview, #reversibility, #latency, #legibility, #trust, #discoverability]
 questions: [#what_is_primary_action, #what_is_safe_to_apply, #what_stays_visible_under_failure]
 qualities: [#clarity, #quiet_feedback, #thin_client]
}

^["cognitive_surface_stack"]{
 layer: #semantic
 reads_from: [#syntactic]
 writes_to: [#semantic]
 teaches: [#operator_roles, #path_topology, #cross_file_navigation, #rename_safety, #brace_physics]
 seed_subsystems: [#lexer, #parser, #types, #query, #instrumentation]
 runtime_subsystems: [#register_bank, #interpret_seed, #run_spw]
 lsp_subsystems: [#analysis, #display, #editing, #navigation, #semantic_tokens, #server_index]
 canon_surfaces: [@register_bank, @dialect_spec, @literate_arch, @tooling]
 depth_map: {
   semantic_tokens: "syntactic — lexer token classification + operator sigil coloring from @register_bank phase definitions"
   hover: "semantic — AST node type + register-bank operator roles + dialect context from @dialect_spec"
   completion: "semantic — scope frame analysis + file-system paths + register access patterns from @register_bank type affinities"
   definition: "semantic — path literal resolution + root graph from workspace manifest"
   rename: "semantic — symbol graph traversal + cascading workspace edits across .spw surfaces"
   diagnostics: "syntactic+semantic — parse errors + broken refs + brace physics (container affinity rules from @register_bank)"
   document_links: "semantic — path references resolved through manifest root + tilde-relative form"
   code_lens: "semantic — annotation metrics + projection state from literate-architecture module shape"
   code_actions: "semantic — AST pattern recognition for trait/binding toggle, wrap-in-frame"
 }
}

^["stream"]{
 # Append entries chronologically. Never edit prior entries.
 # >>[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM] <type> — <content>
 # Types: observe, decide, surprise, revise, blocked, taste, rebase, hygiene, implement, verify, note
 >>[2026-02-20 05:15] observe — SpwLspHandler existing implementation supports hover, outline, and definition, but VSCode extension currently uses regex.
 >>[2026-02-20 05:15] decide — Transition the extension to use vscode-languageclient, connecting via stdio to scripts/lsp/stdio-server.ts.
 >>[2026-02-22 10:10] revise — Added agentic hygiene preflight: mandatory rebase against origin/main and hygiene split for unrelated drift before commit 1.
 >>[2026-03-27 00:45] observe — codebase restructured since plan was filed: LSP now lives in packages/spw-lsp/src/ (handlers/, stdio-server.ts, context.ts, types.ts); seed/parser in packages/spw-seed/src/; extension already has vscode-languageclient ^9.0.1 installed and LanguageClient initialized. Prior commits ~[1]-~[6] are substantially complete.
 >>[2026-03-27 00:46] revise — rebase target updated from lore-era f53934f to current main@3b1747c4. File paths updated throughout. Commits ~[1]-~[6] marked as landed; remaining work starts at ~[7].
 >>[2026-03-27 00:47] decide — for site codebase installation: the LSP must work standalone via `npm run lsp` (already resolved by lsp-lore-upstream-bridge) and the extension must be publishable to VS Code Marketplace. Commit ~[27] should include marketplace metadata.
 >>[2026-03-27 00:48] taste — site codebases will experience spw through the extension first. The quality of hover, completions, and document links directly shapes first impressions. Prioritize correctness over breadth.
 >>[2026-03-27 12:55] observe — Commit 7 (maintain regex DocumentLinkProvider) is obsolete because extension links already moved to LSP ownership. Commits 8 and 9 are effectively landed.
 >>[2026-03-27 13:28] revise — narrow this plan to the editor-reliability lane for site installation. Experimental operator injection is deferred to a separate syntax branch once install/docs/dx surfaces stop moving.
 >>[2026-03-27 13:29] decide — parallelize remaining work into language-service correctness (completion, rename, hover, code action) and editor cleanup/docs (client cleanup, capability docs, release truth).
 >>[2026-03-27 14:22] implement — rewrote branch memory around roots, concept indexing, and recursive improvement; added a branch-local Spw artifact so plan language, capability language, and release claims can share one indexed surface.
 >>[2026-03-27 14:23] taste — recursive improvement here means every new capability should be nameable three ways without drift: code action title, docs snippet, and review vocabulary.
 >>[2026-03-27 18:00] revise — rooted into register-bank.spw, dialect-spec.spw, literate-architecture.spw, and literate-ui.spw as canon surfaces. Added cognitive_surface_stack mapping each LSP handler to the Spw layers it reads: semantic tokens from lexer + register-bank phase defs, hover from AST + operator roles + dialect context, completion from scope frames + register access patterns, etc. The semantic layer this plan builds is the bridge between syntactic parsing and the cognitive surfaces the other three VS Code plans render.
 >>[2026-03-28 09:47] rebase — refreshed baseline to main@b41caa6b and added references/index.spw so LSP protocol, VS Code extension guides, semantic tokens, and TextMate layering stay in the normal reread path.
 >>[2026-03-28 19:18] revise — updated the tooling surface and integration note so editor/LSP quality now has a local doctrine: preview thin-client posture, startup truth, capability truth, quiet feedback, reversible editing, and mindful-growth questions. References now include both web APIs and repo-local quality surfaces.
}

